## 1️⃣ Normal recursion (all ordered sequences)
```java
import java.util.*;

public class DiceNormal {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int sum = 3;
        int faces = 6;
        int[] dp = new int[sum + 1];
        Arrays.fill(dp, -1);

        System.out.println(find(sum, dp, faces)); // Output: 4
    }

    private static int find(int sum, int[] dp, int faces) {
        if (sum == 0) return 1;
        if (dp[sum] != -1) return dp[sum];

        int ans = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i <= faces; i++) {
            if (sum - i >= 0) {
                ans += find(sum - i, dp, faces);
            }
        }
        return dp[sum] = ans;
    }
}
```
👉 Counts ordered sequences (e.g. `[1,2]` and `[2,1]` both included).

