## 2️⃣ Don’t repeat the combination (skip duplicates)
```java
import java.util.*;

public class DiceNoDuplicates {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int sum = 3;
        int faces = 6;
        int[][] dp = new int[sum + 1][faces + 2];
        for (int[] row : dp) Arrays.fill(row, -1);

        System.out.println(find(sum, 1, dp, faces)); // Output: 3
    }

    private static int find(int sum, int minFace, int[][] dp, int faces) {
        if (sum == 0) return 1;
        if (dp[sum][minFace] != -1) return dp[sum][minFace];

        int ans = 0;
        for (int i = minFace; i <= faces; i++) {
            if (sum - i >= 0) {
                ans += find(sum - i, i, dp, faces); // enforce non-decreasing order
            }
        }
        return dp[sum][minFace] = ans;
    }
}
```
👉 `[1,2]` is counted, `[2,1]` is skipped.

