## 3️⃣ Face changes (no face can be reused)
```java
import java.util.*;

public class DiceNoRepeatFace {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int sum = 6;
        int faces = 6;
        int[][] dp = new int[sum + 1][faces + 2];
        for (int[] row : dp) Arrays.fill(row, -1);

        System.out.println(count(sum, 1, faces, dp)); // Output: 4
    }

    private static int count(int sum, int startFace, int faces, int[][] dp) {
        if (sum == 0) return 1;
        if (startFace > faces) return 0;
        if (dp[sum][startFace] != -1) return dp[sum][startFace];

        int ans = 0;
        for (int i = startFace; i <= faces; i++) {
            if (sum - i >= 0) {
                ans += count(sum - i, i + 1, faces, dp); // move forward, no reuse
            }
        }
        return dp[sum][startFace] = ans;
    }
}
```
👉 Each face can only appear once in a combination.

