## 4️⃣ Add the number of dice used (track dice count)
```java
import java.util.*;

public class DiceWithCount {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int sum = 6;
        int faces = 6;
        int maxDice = 3; // constraint: use at most 3 dice

        int[][][] dp = new int[sum + 1][faces + 2][maxDice + 1];
        for (int[][] mat : dp) for (int[] row : mat) Arrays.fill(row, -1);

        System.out.println(count(sum, 1, faces, maxDice, dp));
    }

    private static int count(int sum, int startFace, int faces, int diceLeft, int[][][] dp) {
        if (sum == 0 && diceLeft >= 0) return 1;
        if (sum < 0 || startFace > faces || diceLeft == 0) return 0;
        if (dp[sum][startFace][diceLeft] != -1) return dp[sum][startFace][diceLeft];

        int ans = 0;
        for (int i = startFace; i <= faces; i++) {
            ans += count(sum - i, i + 1, faces, diceLeft - 1, dp);
        }
        return dp[sum][startFace][diceLeft] = ans;
    }
}
```
👉 Adds a constraint on the number of dice used (e.g. “at most 3 dice”).

